{"copyright":{"thirdPartyPermissionsProduced":false,"disclosedToPublic":false,"containsIndication":false,"publisherPermissionOrRightsToDistribute":false,"belongsToUsGov":false,"determinationType":"PUBLIC_USE_PERMITTED","thirdPartyContentCondition":"NOT_SET","belongsToContractor":false,"disclosedInvention":false,"submissionId":20110008446,"containsThirdPartyMaterial":false,"belongsToPublisher":false,"id":"3c57dad7319b4c5695679ed32cb5f625","belongsToAuthors":false},"subjectCategories":["Man/System Technology And Life Support"],"exportControl":{"isExportControl":"NO","submissionId":20110008446,"ear":"NO","id":"fd4a45a96291492295442410154582fc","itar":"NO"},"distributionDate":"2019-07-12T00:00:00.0000000+00:00","otherReportNumbers":["JSC-CN-23094","Report Number: JSC-CN-23094"],"fundingNumbers":[{"number":"WBS 903184.04.20.02.02.01","submissionId":20110008446,"id":"ee996b6ccfbe4c4ab779d7490b216fa1","type":"WBS"},{"number":"NNX10CF24P","submissionId":20110008446,"id":"2a5aa00b7f6646e08021ef04f86e1c04","type":"CONTRACT_GRANT"}],"title":"Carbon Dioxide Control System for a Mars Space Suit Life Support System","stiType":"OTHER","distribution":"PUBLIC","submittedDate":"2013-08-25T09:07:00.0000000+00:00","authorAffiliations":[{"sequence":0,"submissionId":20110008446,"meta":{"author":{"name":"Alptekin, Gokhan"},"organization":{"name":"TDA Research, Inc.","location":"Wheat Ridge, CO, United States"}},"id":"99c7728af5b340bd83af16dca9db1b8c"},{"sequence":1,"submissionId":20110008446,"meta":{"author":{"name":"Jayaraman, Ambalavanan"},"organization":{"name":"TDA Research, Inc.","location":"Wheat Ridge, CO, United States"}},"id":"0894e1e94f7e4555be72700bea2e986a"},{"sequence":2,"submissionId":20110008446,"meta":{"author":{"name":"Copeland, Robert"},"organization":{"name":"TDA Research, Inc.","location":"Wheat Ridge, CO, United States"}},"id":"cdb957ac31a140c2abf953eff2031ee2"},{"sequence":3,"submissionId":20110008446,"meta":{"author":{"name":"Parker, Amanda"},"organization":{"name":"TDA Research, Inc.","location":"Wheat Ridge, CO, United States"}},"id":"33a7ea8c754b432389223b4968b3925d"},{"sequence":4,"submissionId":20110008446,"meta":{"author":{"name":"Paul, Heather L."},"organization":{"name":"NASA Johnson Space Center","location":"Houston, TX, United States"}},"id":"0864596286c44a8b8749a83dcc17fda0"}],"stiTypeDetails":"Other","technicalReviewType":"TECHNICAL_REVIEW_TYPE_NONE","modified":"2025-08-31T18:39:21.7150190+00:00","id":20110008446,"legacyMeta":{"__type":"LegacyMetaIndex, StrivesApi.ServiceModel","accessionNumber":""},"created":"2013-08-25T09:07:00.0000000+00:00","center":{"code":"JSC","name":"Johnson Space Center","id":"dd46994b91a94cb2a2722617cbbadc55"},"onlyAbstract":false,"sensitiveInformation":2,"abstract":"Carbon dioxide (CO2) control during Extravehicular Activities (EVAs) on Mars will be challenging. Lithium hydroxide (LiOH) canisters have impractical logistics penalties, and regenerable metal oxide (MetOx) canisters weigh too much. Cycling bed systems and permeable membranes that are regenerable in space vacuum cannot vent on Mars due to the high partial pressure of CO2 in the atmosphere. Although sweep gas regeneration is under investigation, the feasibility, logistics penalties, and failure modes associated with this technique have not been fully determined. TDA Research, Inc. is developing a durable, high-capacity regenerable adsorbent that can remove CO2 from the space suit ventilation loop. The system design allows sorbent regeneration at or above 6 torr, eliminating the potential for Martian atmosphere to leak into the regeneration bed and into the ventilation loop. Regeneration during EVA minimizes the amount of consumables to be brought from Earth and makes the mission more affordable, while providing great operational flexibility during EVA. The feasibility of the concept has been demonstrated in a series of bench-scale experiments and a preliminary system analysis. This paper presents the latest results from these sorbent and system development efforts.","isLessonsLearned":false,"disseminated":"DOCUMENT_AND_METADATA","meetings":[{"country":"United States","submissionId":20110008446,"endDate":"2011-07-21T00:00:00.0000000+00:00","name":"41st International Conference on Environmental Systems","location":"Portland, OR","id":"7e77b78bedee4dacaf3fc3c9736a1a9f","startDate":"2011-07-17T00:00:00.0000000+00:00"}],"publications":[{"submissionId":20110008446,"id":"9a4dddf1817049c7adb6cf7dd4d5dc68","publicationDate":"2011-01-01T00:00:00.0000000+00:00"}],"status":"CURATED","related":[],"downloads":[{"draft":false,"mimetype":"application/pdf","name":"20110008446.pdf","type":"STI","links":{"original":"/api/citations/20110008446/downloads/20110008446.pdf","pdf":"/api/citations/20110008446/downloads/20110008446.pdf","fulltext":"/api/citations/20110008446/downloads/20110008446.txt"}}],"downloadsAvailable":true,"index":"submissions-2026-11-05-06-21"}